{
 "provenance": "Imported 2026-09-16 from the original config set. levels[].growthsRequired is SimGame3PlantUpgrade.upgradeCost on the row for level N: the requirement to raise that plant from level N to N+1, which is why the 39 level-3 rows carry none -- level 3 is terminal. It is NOT a currency and NOT a quantity of crop -- it is a COUNT OF TIMES the plant has been grown. The client compares it against plants[id].recordCount (SimGame3Manager:GetPlantUpNoticeById -> \"upgradeCost <= GetPlantRecordCount(plantId)\"), never the spendable stock plants[id].count, and the original's own strings settle the unit: the failure toast SG3PlantUpTips reads cn \"\u7d2f\u79ef\u79cd\u690d\u7684\u6b21\u6570\u4e0d\u8db3\" / jp \"\u690d\u7269\u3092\u690d\u3048\u305f\u56de\u6570\u304c\u8db3\u308a\u307e\u305b\u3093\" -- \"the accumulated NUMBER OF TIMES planted is insufficient\" -- and the progress label SG3PlantRecord is cn \"\u7d2f\u8ba1\u79cd\u51fa\" / jp \"\u7d2f\u8a08\u6210\u679c\". risePercent is hundredths of a percent (2500 = +25%). The affected business type is SimGame3Plant.country 1-5 mapped onto Inspiring/Diligent/Brave/Informed/Unfettered, which agrees 39/39 with the effectText already in farm-level-data.json. plots is SimGame3Field: the farm opens with plot 1 (isDefaultUnlock) and the other eleven are reclaimed with KNOWLEDGE (consume). Generated inline (no scripts/ importer: the authoring agent was scoped to lib/farm*).",
